{"id":"4d97706b34d0bf564ab091bb16f2da036c1b8064","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1000443/qualcomms-new-elite-sound-chip-might-finally-deliver-the-wi-fi-earbud-dream","title":"Qualcomm’s new ‘Elite’ sound chip might finally deliver the Wi-Fi earbud dream","site_name":"TechURLs","source":"The Verge","byline":"Sean Hollister","excerpt":"Also, they can power earbuds with cameras.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div><div><p><a href=\"/authors/sean-hollister\"><img alt=\"Sean Hollister\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96 2x\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=96\"></a></p><div><p><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span id=\"follow-author-standard_article_details-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MzQz\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></svg></span></span><span>Sean Hollister</span></span></span></p> <p><span>is a senior editor and founding member of The Verge who covers gadgets, games, and toys. He spent 15 years editing the likes of CNET, Gizmodo, and Engadget.</span></p></div></div><div id=\"zephr-anchor\"><p>What if your wireless earbuds — or audio glasses — could stream high-quality lossless audio that <em>doesn’t</em> cut out when you leave your phone on the bedside charger or buried in the couch? Qualcomm’s new <a href=\"https://www.qualcomm.com/audio/products/snapdragon-sound-elite-gen-2\">Snapdragon Sound Elite Gen 2</a> is its first to integrate “micro-power Wi-Fi 6E” right into the chip, so they can connect directly to your home Wi-Fi network, and from there to the cloud.</p><div><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100\" data-pswp-height=\"308\" data-pswp-width=\"339\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"Qualcomm’s old whitepaper shows that it originally required two chips for Wi-Fi earbuds. Now, Wi-Fi is integrated into the main chip.\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 639px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 700px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=256 256w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400 2400w\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/image-26.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400\"></a></p></div><p>If that sounds like a familiar promise, it’s probably because Qualcomm promised something similar back in 2023 <a href=\"/2023/10/24/23930039/qualcomm-snapdragon-sound-s7-pro-announced-earbuds-wifi\">with the “S7 Pro sound platform”</a> and its Expanded Personal Area Network (XPAN) tech, saying that Wi-Fi earbuds can do what Bluetooth alone cannot. Namely, 24-bit 96kHz lossless audio that can’t fit into Bluetooth’s meager bandwidth.</p><p>But that old 7-series platform required <em>a separate Wi-Fi chip</em> to give you Wi-Fi earbuds, and it seems that wasn’t a winning formula for getting makers of incredibly tiny devices to adopt the tech! In fact, we’ve only ever heard of one: <a href=\"/news/622452/xiaomi-buds-5-pro-are-the-first-to-deliver-on-qualcomms-promise-of-wi-fi-earbuds\">Xiaomi’s 2025 Buds 5 Pro</a>, which didn’t get a global release.</p><div><div><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100\" data-pswp-height=\"720\" data-pswp-width=\"1280\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 639px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 700px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=256 256w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400 2400w\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/assets_2026_09_1789673099_Snapdragon-Sound-Elite-Gen-2-Highlight-Image-Embargo-Sep-23-930am-HT-1230pm-PT.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400\"></a></p></div><p><cite>Image: Qualcomm</cite></p></div><p>Now that Wi-Fi no longer requires an extra chip, perhaps the idea can take off. Qualcomm says the Elite is also 30 percent smaller, consumes up to 40 percent less power, and has twice the AI processing capabilities of the previous gen chip, all of which should be music to device makers’ ears.</p><p>So far, Qualcomm says it’s working with HP on one specific unnamed product, is “working closely with Bose,” and is “pioneering a new category of intelligent hearables” (read: earbuds with built-in cameras) with Cleer.</p><div><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,0,100,100\" data-pswp-height=\"1080\" data-pswp-width=\"1920\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"The camera earbuds.\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 639px) 100vw, (max-width: 1023px) 50vw, 700px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=256 256w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400 2400w\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/vlcsnap-2026-09-24-16h35m50s149.png?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&w=2400\"></a></p></div><div><p><span><strong>Follow topics and authors</strong> from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates.</span></p><ul><li id=\"follow-author-article_footer-dmcyOmF1dGhvclByb2ZpbGU6MzQz\"><span aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-haspopup=\"true\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><span><span><svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 9 9\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"Follow\"><path d=\"M5 0H4V4H0V5H4V9H5V5H9V4H5V0Z\" /></sv